{"role": "tool", "content": "command: hops --help\nstdout: Usage: hops [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...\n\n  Hopsworks CLI — for humans and LLMs.\n\n  Run `hops setup` to authenticate on a new machine.\n\nOptions:\n  -v, --version           Show the version and exit.\n  --host TEXT             Hopsworks host URL (overrides config).\n  --api-key TEXT          API key (overrides config).\n  --project TEXT          Project name (overrides config).\n  --verify / --no-verify  Verify the Hopsworks TLS certificate (hostname\n                          verification). Use --no-verify to skip verification\n                          when a cluster serves a self-signed or IP-SAN-\n                          mismatched certificate. Maps to the SDK's\n                          hopsworks.login(hostname_verification=...);\n                          overridden by HOPSWORKS_HOSTNAME_VERIFICATION when\n                          that env var is set.\n  --json                  Output as JSON (for LLMs).\n  -h, --help              Show this message and exit.\n\nCommands:\n  agent           Python agent deployment commands.\n  alert           Alert and alert-receiver commands.\n  app             Python app commands.\n  context         Emit a Markdown or JSON summary of the active project.\n  datasource      Data source (storage connector) commands.\n  deployment      Model serving deployment commands.\n  env             Python environment commands (list, clone, install).\n  fg              Feature group commands.\n  files           File-system commands on HopsFS (list, mkdir, upload,...\n  fv              Feature view commands.\n  init            Scaffold the Hopsworks Claude Code skill bundle.\n  job             Job commands.\n  login           Authenticate non-interactively with an existing API key.\n  model           Model registry commands.\n  project         List and switch Hopsworks projects.\n  search          Search the Hopsworks feature store (project-scoped by...\n  setup           Authenticate with Hopsworks and cache an API key in...\n  skills          Discover the Hopsworks skills (Markdown playbooks)...\n  sql             Run an ad-hoc SQL query.\n  superset        Superset commands (datasets, charts, dashboards).\n  td              Training dataset commands.\n  transformation  Transformation function commands.\n  trino           Trino commands (query, catalogs, schemas, tables).\n  update          Print the command to upgrade the ``hopsworks`` package.\n\nstderr: \nreturncode: 0", "injected": false, "name": "bash", "tool_call_id": "VYMavr8yn"}
